256 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /H2
  /P 255 0 R
  /T (This kind of app architecture was the most common one before the rise of front-end frameworks like React, Vue or Angular. You may find it old-fashioned, but it's still widely used today for small to medium web applications, as it's simple to implement and maintain. This kind of architecture is also really similar to API backends that are really common today, so it's important to understand how it works.)
  /K [10 257 0 R]
  /Pg 642 0 R
>>
endobj

